{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-27-1","title":"Job 27:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job protests his sincerity. 8 The hypocrite is without hope. 11 The blessings which the wicked have are turned into curses.</p>\n<p>Job. Nu 23:7; 24:3,15; Ps 49:4; 78:2; Pr 26:7 continued. Heb. added to take up.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-2","title":"Job 27:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>God liveth. Nu 14:21; Ru 3:13; 1Sa 14:39,45; 20:21; 25:26,34; 2Sa 2:27 1Ki 17:1; 18:15; Jer 4:2; 5:2; 12:16; Eze 33:11 taken. 10:3; 34:5; Isa 40:27 vexed my soul. Heb. made my soul bitter. Ru 1:20,21; 2Ki 4:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-3","title":"Job 27:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the spirit of God. that is, the breath which God gave him. Ge 2:7; Isa 2:22; Ac 17:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-4","title":"Job 27:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>13:7; 34:6; Joh 8:55; 2Co 11:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-5","title":"Job 27:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>justify. 32:3; 42:7; De 25:1; Pr 17:15; Ga 2:11 I will not. 2:9; 13:15; 29:14; 2Co 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-6","title":"Job 27:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I hold fast. 2:3; Ps 18:20-23; Pr 4:13 my heart. Ac 24:16; 2Co 12:11; 1Jo 3:20,21 so long as I live. Heb. from my days.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-7","title":"Job 27:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>1Sa 25:26; 2Sa 18:32; Da 4:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-8","title":"Job 27:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>11:20; 13:16; 15:34; 20:5; 31:3; Isa 33:14,15; Mt 16:26; 23:14 Mr 8:36,37; Lu 9:25; 12:20,21; 1Ti 6:9,10; Jas 5:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-9","title":"Job 27:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Will God. 35:12,13; Ps 18:41; 66:18; 109:7; Pr 1:28; 28:9; Isa 1:15 Jer 11:11; 14:12; Eze 8:18; Mic 3:4; Zec 7:13; Joh 9:31; Jas 4:3 his cry. Ho 7:14; Lu 13:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-10","title":"Job 27:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>delight. 22:26,27; Ps 37:4; 43:4; Hab 3:18 will he always. Ps 78:34-36; Mt 13:21; Lu 18:1; Ac 10:2; Eph 6:18; 1Th 5:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-11","title":"Job 27:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>teach. 4:3,4; 6:10; Isa 8:11 by the hand. or, being in the hand, etc. that which. 32:8-10; De 4:5; Ps 71:17; Ac 20:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-12","title":"Job 27:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>ye yourselves. 21:28-30; Ec 8:14; 9:1-3 altogether. 6:25-29; 13:4-9; 16:3; 17:2; 19:2,3; 21:3; 26:2-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-13","title":"Job 27:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the portion. 20:29; 31:3; Ps 11:6; Ec 8:13; Isa 3:11; 2Pe 2:9 the heritage. 15:20-35; 20:19-29; Ps 12:5; Pr 22:22,23; Mal 3:5; Jas 5:4-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-14","title":"Job 27:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>children. 21:11,12; De 28:32,41; 2Ki 9:7,8; 10:6-10; Es 5:11; 9:5-10 Ps 109:13; Ho 9:13,14; Lu 23:29 his offspring. 1Sa 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-15","title":"Job 27:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Those. 1Ki 14:10,11; 16:3,4; 21:21-24 his widows. Ps 78:64; Jer 22:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-16","title":"Job 27:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>heap up. 22:24; 1Ki 10:27; Hab 2:6; Zec 9:3 prepare raiment.D'Herbelot tells us, that Bokhten, an illustrious poet of Cufah, in the 9th century, had so many presents made him, that at his death he was found possessed of 100 suits of clothes, 200 shirts, and 500 turbans.</p>\n<p>Mt 6:19; Jas 5:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-17","title":"Job 27:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>but the just. Pr 13:22; 28:8; Ec 2:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-18","title":"Job 27:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>as a moth. 8:14,15; Isa 51:8 as a booth. Isa 1:8; 38:12; La 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-19","title":"Job 27:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>shall lie. 14:13-15; 21:23-26,30; 30:23 gathered. Ge 49:10; Jer 8:2; Mt 3:12; 23:37 he openeth. 20:7-9; Ps 58:9; 73:19,20 he is not. 8:22; 14:10,12; 24:24; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-20","title":"Job 27:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Terrors. 15:21; 18:11; 22:16; Ps 18:4; 42:7; 69:14,15; Jon 2:3 a tempest. 20:23; 21:18; Ex 12:29; 2Ki 19:35; Da 5:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-21","title":"Job 27:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>east wind. Jer 18:17; Ho 13:15 a storm. Ex 9:23-25; Ps 11:6; 58:9; 83:15; Na 1:3-8; Mt 7:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-22","title":"Job 27:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>For God. Ex 9:14; De 32:23; Jos 10:11 not spare. De 29:20; Eze 9:5,6; Ro 8:32; 2Pe 2:4,5 he would fain flee. Heb. in fleeing he would flee. 20:24; Ex 14:25-28; Jud 4:17-21; Isa 10:3; Am 2:14; 9:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-27-23","title":"Job 27:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>clap. Es 9:22-25; Pr 11:10; La 2:15; Re 18:20 hiss him. 1Ki 9:8; Jer 19:8; Mic 6:16; Zep 2:15</p>"}]}